  "english": "[March]\n26. Sunday. Tone 1 [AH]. Easter (Zatik). Day of the Resurrection\nof Christ our God. See\naccording to the order in the First Volume.\n\n[April]\n7. Friday. Tone 6 [GY]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy\nVirgin Mary.\n\nMay\n14. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Coming of the Holy Spirit (Pentecost).\nEve of the Fast of Elijah.\n21. Sunday. Tone 1 [AH]. First Sunday. Beginning of the Sundays\nof the Resurrection. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 1 [AD]:\n\"Who came for salvation.\" See according to\nthe order in the First Volume.\n\n[July]\n2. Sunday. Tone 3 [BZ]. Vardavar (Transfiguration). The season\nof eating [non-fasting] is five weeks. See in the First\nVolume up to the Friday of the third week,\nwhich is nineteen days; and on the Saturday\ncome here, and celebrate these feasts listed below,\nwhich are after the eight days of the Theophany (Nativity).\n22. Saturday. Tone 8 [DZ]. Bishop Peter,\nBishop Blaise, and Abisolom the Deacon.\n25. Sunday. Tone 7 [DK]. Fourth Sunday. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 4 [BK]: \"Who [the] heavenly host.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [DK]:\n\"When they came,\" and \"The angel descended.\"\n24. Monday. Tone 1 [AH]. Anton the Anchorite.\n25. Tuesday. Tone 2 [AK]. King Theodosius, and\nthe Children of Ephesus.\n27. Thursday. Tone 4 [BK]. Cyriacus and Julitta,\nand Gordius, Polyeuctus, and\nGrigoris. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 5 [DZ]: \"Holy art Thou,\nLord of hosts.\"\n29. Saturday. Tone 6 [GK]. Patriarchs Athanasius\nand Cyril, and Gregory the\nTheologian.\n30. Sunday. Tone 5 [DZ]. Fifth Sunday. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 4 [BK]:\n\"Unoriginate God.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [DZ]:\n\"The women anticipating.\"\n31. Monday. Tone 7 [DK]. Vahan of Goghtn,\nand Eugenia the Virgin, etc.\nPatristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 7 [DK]: \"To Thee, O God.\"\n\n[August]\n1. Tuesday. Tone 1 [AH]. Tryphon, Barsama, and\nOnuphrius the Anchorites.\n3. Thursday. Tone 3 [BZ]. Eugenius, Macarius,\netc. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 7 [DK]: \"Who wonderfully.\"\n5. Saturday. Tone 5 [GZ]. The Holy Ecumenical Council of Ephesus\nof the two hundred Patriarchs.\n6. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK]. Sixth Sunday. Eve\nof the Fast of the Assumption of the Mother of God. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 5 [GZ]:\n\"We glorify Thee.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [GK]:\n\"With the divine tomb.\"\n7. Monday. Tone 5 [DZ]. Fast of the Holy Mother of\nGod. Patristic Fast Hymn [Harts Salts] Tone 3 [BZ]: \"Who awesome.\"\n13. Sunday. Tone 5 [DZ]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of\nGod. The season of eating [non-fasting] is four\nweeks.\n23. Wednesday. Tone 7 [DK]. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 4 [BK]: \"The captive\nchildren.\"\n26. Saturday. Tone 2 [AK]. Thomas the Apostle.\nFor the rest of this season, see according to the order in the\nFirst Volume, keeping the order of the place...\n\nSeptember\n2. Saturday. Tone 1 [AH]. Apostles James and\nSimon. Read the Lections and the Gospel\nof the Tuesday of the Fast of Saint James.\n3. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Fourth Sunday. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 5 [DZ]: \"Glorified Son.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [AK]: \"The risen Lord.\"\n4. Monday. Tone 3 [BZ]. Andrew the Commander and\nhis army, etc.\n5. Tuesday. Tone 4 [BK]. Adrian and his wife\nAnatolia, etc. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 2 [AK]: \"Holy God.\"\n7. Thursday. Tone 6 [GK]. Abraham and Khoren,\nCosmas and Damian, and\nAsadour (Adeodatus) the Martyr. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 6 [GK]: \"Who on high.\"\n8. Friday. Tone 5 [DZ]. Feast of the Nativity of the Holy\nVirgin from Anna.\n9. Saturday. Tone 7 [DK]. The Holy Ecumenical Council of Nicaea,\nof the three hundred and eighteen\nPatriarchs.\n10. Sunday. Tone 1 [AH]. Fifth Sunday. Eve\nof the Fast of the Holy Cross. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [AD]:\n\"With the women.\"",
